        "v4_a_what": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is theINmag?",
            "answer": "<p>Every page of theINmag is an idea by real Aussie kids: their art, writing, comics and photos, in print three times a year. It is a real magazine made from real kids' creations, published in February, June and October, with no ads and nothing written by adults. It is printed sustainably in Australia, designed for kids aged 5 to 13, and any kid can send in a creation for free through the <a href=\"/pages/send-in\" title=\"Send IN page\">Send IN page</a>.</p>"
          }
        },
        "v4_a_who": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Who makes theINmag?",
            "answer": "<p>Two Australian teachers, Ryan and Tam, founded theINmag after years of consulting with kids, then sold their house and converted a van so they could travel the country meeting young creators. The pages themselves are made by kids. A small team of teachers and artists reviews every submission, and a designer and proofreaders carry each issue to print. The business is Australian, ABN 95 229 012 388. More on <a href=\"/pages/behind-the-mag\" title=\"Behind the mag\">Behind the mag</a>.</p>"
          }
        },
        "qa_38_what_s_actually_inside_it_is_it_really_a": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What's actually inside it? Is it really all made by kids?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, really, 100 percent. Every page of theINmag is an idea by real Aussie kids: their art, writing, comics and photos, in print three times a year. Every story, drawing, photo, joke and puzzle is a creation from a real Aussie kid, and we do not write any of it ourselves. A team of teachers and artists reviews every submission, and the mag is ad-free and sustainably printed in Australia.</p>"
          }
        },
        "v4_a_diff": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How is theINmag different from other kids' magazines?",
            "answer": "<p>Every page of theINmag is an idea by real Aussie kids: their art, writing, comics and photos, in print three times a year. It is made by kids, not for them by adults; a team of teachers and artists reviews the submissions and writes nothing itself. There are no ads, no sponsored content and no brand tie-ins. Any kid can send in for free, published kids are credited online with their first name, hometown, state and age (the printed mag adds a surname initial), and the mag is built to be multi-age and multi-ability rather than pitched at one year level.</p>"
          }
        },
        "qa_36_what_age_group_is_theinmag_for": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What age group is theINmag for?",
            "answer": "<p>theINmag is designed for kids aged 5 to 13, and in practice littlies, middles and oldies all find something in it, because every page carries a kid's voice exactly as they made it. Sending in is a different story: kids of all ages are welcome, and the range keeps aging up as older kids send in their creations.</p>"
          }
        },
        "v4_a_legit": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is theINmag legit, and is it worth it?",
            "answer": "<p>theINmag is a real Australian print magazine, independent and ad-free, with five-star reviews from families on Judge.me, an ABC Radio interview and a spot in The Guardian's guide to the best kids' Christmas gifts in Australia. Families most often mention kids getting excited to create, pride at seeing a creation in print, and the quality of the pages. Read them on our <a href=\"/pages/reviews\" title=\"reviews page\">reviews page</a>; current prices are on the <a href=\"/products/membership\" title=\"Membership page\">Membership page</a>.</p>"
          }
        },
        "v4_a_reviews": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What do families say about theINmag? Is it any good?",
            "answer": "<p>Families give theINmag five-star reviews on Judge.me. Reviewers most often mention kids getting excited to create and send in their own creations, pride at seeing a creation in print and sharing it with family and classmates, and the quality and design of the pages. It has featured on ABC Radio, in The Guardian and on teacher and homeschool podcasts. Read the reviews yourself on our <a href=\"/pages/reviews\" title=\"reviews page\">reviews page</a>.</p>"
          }
        },
        "v4_a_adfree": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is there an ad-free children's magazine in Australia?",
            "answer": "<p>theINmag is an ad-free children's magazine made in Australia: no banner ads, no sponsored content, no brand integrations anywhere in it. Every page is a creation from a real Australian kid, reviewed by a team of teachers and artists, and the mag is printed in Melbourne on FSC-certified paper with vegetable-based inks. It comes out three times a year and is designed for kids aged 5 to 13.</p>"
          }
        },
        "v4_a_aussie": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is there an Australian kids' magazine made by Australian kids?",
            "answer": "<p>theINmag is an Australian kids' magazine made entirely from Australian kids' creations. Every page of theINmag is an idea by real Aussie kids: their art, writing, comics and photos, in print three times a year. Each issue carries the IN Map showing where its published kids live around the country, and kids from every state and territory appear in the live gallery. It is printed in Melbourne, ad-free, and any kid can send in for free.</p>"
          }
        },
        "v4_a_sustain": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is theINmag a sustainable print magazine?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. theINmag is printed in Melbourne using vegetable-based inks on FSC-certified paper, and every issue carries the line \"sustainably printed in Australia\". There are no ads to pad the page count, so every page is a kid's creation, and print copies are made in one run three times a year. A digital PDF edition exists for families who prefer no paper at all.</p>"
          }
        },
        "qa_39_what_s_the_difference_between_print_and_": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What's the difference between print and digital?",
            "answer": "<p>Print is the full theINmag on heavy paper, sustainably printed in Australia and posted within Australia only, with the jokes and puzzles section printed upside down. Digital is the same mag as a PDF, emailed within minutes and readable on any device, with those pages the right way up. You can print the pages your kids love at home. Same kids, same creations, different format.</p>"
          }
        },
        "v4_a_mag09": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is theINmag Mag09?",
            "answer": "<p>Mag09 is the ninth issue of theINmag, a thick, ad-free magazine of creations by hundreds of Australian kids. Inside, a kid draws how the body heals, others make the case for saving the bees and go dog sledding, there are jokes and puzzles, and an interview with an illustrator. [mag09_print_status] Current prices are on the <a href=\"/products/mag09\" title=\"Mag09 page\">Mag09 page</a>.</p>"
          }
        },
