        "qa_01_how_does_my_kid_get_published_in_theinma": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How does my kid get published in theINmag?",
            "answer": "<p>Head to our <a href=\"/pages/send-in\" title=\"Send IN page\">Send IN page</a>, upload the creation and have a grown-up tick the consent box. It is free, and kids of all ages are welcome. A real human on our team of teachers and artists reviews every submission, and nothing is ever auto-published. Hundreds of kids' creations make it into each issue, and the number one thing we look for is effort, not polish, so send in something your kid genuinely loves.</p>"
          }
        },
        "v4_a_where": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Where can kids get their writing or art published in a real magazine?",
            "answer": "<p>theINmag publishes kids' creations in a real printed magazine, for free, and kids of all ages are welcome. A story, drawing, comic, photo, joke, recipe, song or something they built goes in through our <a href=\"/pages/send-in\" title=\"Send IN page\">Send IN page</a>, a grown-up ticks consent, and a human team reviews every submission. Selected creations are printed, and creations are shared to the <a href=\"/pages/gallery\" title=\"live gallery\">live gallery</a>, credited online with their first name, hometown, state and age (the printed mag adds a surname initial).</p>"
          }
        },
        "qa_02_where_and_how_do_we_send_in_a_drawing_or": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Where and how do we send in a drawing or story?",
            "answer": "<p>Head to our <a href=\"/pages/send-in\">Send IN page</a>. Upload your child's creation there, whether it is a drawing, story, photo, joke or puzzle. It is free, it takes a few minutes, and a real human reviews every single submission. Nothing is ever auto-published. You will see a celebration screen once you hit submit, and if the creation is selected for print and you shared a parent email, we will be in touch before the issue drops.</p>"
          }
        },
        "v4_send_what_can": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What can kids send in to theINmag?",
            "answer": "<p>Just about anything they have made: writing, drawings, comics, photos, jokes, facts, puzzles, songs, recipes, hobbies, and things they built like shelters, veggie patches, sculptures or a really great box. Photograph it with a phone or iPad in bright light, save the largest file you can and add two or three sentences about it. For the gallery, no copyrighted characters, real faces or school names.</p>"
          }
        },
        "qa_03_can_my_grandkids_send_in_their_creations": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can my grandkids send in their creations too?",
            "answer": "<p>Absolutely, grandkids are very welcome. Any Aussie kid roughly 4 to 16 can send in a creation through our <a href=\"/pages/send-in\">Send IN page</a>, and it is free. You do not need to be the parent to help them submit, and a real person on our team reviews everything that comes in. If you would like to make it extra special, plenty of grandparents pair a Send IN with a gift <a href=\"/products/membership\">Membership</a> so the mag lands in the letterbox too.</p>"
          }
        },
        "qa_04_is_my_child_too_old_or_too_young_to_subm": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is my child too old or too young to submit?",
            "answer": "<p>Almost certainly not. theINmag is open to Aussie kids roughly 4 to 16, and the range has been aging up as older kids keep sending in creations. We celebrate all ages and all abilities, so if your child has made something they are proud of, we would love to see it.</p>"
          }
        },
        "qa_05_what_happens_after_we_hit_submit": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What happens after we hit submit?",
            "answer": "<p>First, a celebration screen. Then a real person on our team of teachers and artists reviews the submission. We never auto-publish anything. If the creation is chosen for print and you left a parent email on the form, we email you before the issue drops. The parent email is optional, so we only contact families who shared it. So many creations arrive for each issue that we cannot reply to every submission individually, so look for your child's creation in the <a href=\"/pages/gallery\" title=\"live gallery\">live gallery</a>. Published kids do not receive a free copy; a Membership or a single issue is the surest way to hold the page.</p>"
          }
        },
        "qa_06_what_if_our_creation_isn_t_picked": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What if our creation isn't picked?",
            "answer": "<p>Not every creation makes print, because there are more incredible kids than there are pages. Creations are shared to our <a href=\"/pages/gallery\" title=\"live gallery\">live gallery</a>, which shows live submissions from recent months filtered by art, writing, photos, puzzles, hobbies and wonderings, so other kids still get to see what your child made. Two things help next time: serious effort, and sending in lots of different creations across the year.</p>"
          }
        },
        "qa_07_is_this_safe_for_my_kid": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is this safe for my kid?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Published kids are credited online with their first name, hometown, state and age (the printed mag adds a surname initial). We never show full names, schools, addresses, contact details or faces in photos. A parent or guardian must say yes before anything is sent, and the form is for adults only. A real person reviews every submission, nothing is auto-published, and you can ask us to take a creation down at any time. The details are in our <a href=\"/pages/child-safety-terms-conditions-privacy-policy\" title=\"child safety and privacy policy\">child safety and privacy policy</a>.</p>"
          }
        },
        "qa_08_can_i_take_my_kid_s_creation_down_later": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I take my kid's creation down later?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, anytime. Email <a href=\"mailto:heyhey@theinmag.com.au\">heyhey@theinmag.com.au</a> and we will remove the creation from the website and <a href=\"/pages/gallery\">gallery</a>, no questions asked. Print and digital copies that have already been published cannot be recalled, but nothing future-facing stays up once you ask us to take it down.</p>"
          }
        },
        "v4_send_owns": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Who owns my child's creation after it's published?",
            "answer": "<p>Your child does. theINmag receives a non-exclusive, royalty-free, worldwide, perpetual licence, so the child can reuse the creation anywhere else. Accepted creations may appear in print, on the website and social channels, in marketing and on products such as prints or cards, with any proceeds funding future ad-free issues. How long submission records are kept is set out in our <a href=\"/pages/child-safety-terms-conditions-privacy-policy\" title=\"child safety and privacy policy\">child safety and privacy policy</a>.</p>"
          }
        },
